      "kind": {
        "text": "Established on the `cas-certificate` route, in the geometry family: a Nullstellensatz-style cofactor identity `conclusion = sum_i cofactor_i * generator_i` over the hypothesis ideal, re-derived by polynomial addition and multiplication alone. This fact is filed deliberately alongside F:geometry-centroid-divides-medians and F:geometry-parallelogram-diagonals-bisect, which DO need a non-degeneracy condition. The distinction is measured by the certifier (it tries the empty condition set first and reports what it used), not asserted in prose -- which is the point, because a mechanised geometry proof that silently assumes non-degeneracy is wrong in the direction that manufactures theorems.",
